        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "Two houses on a grid"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Two houses are at (2, 1) and (5, 5) on a town grid. A cable runs straight between them. How long is it, and where is its middle?"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "distance formula",
          "Pythagoras",
          "mid-point",
          "section formula",
          "trisection",
          "centroid"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "The distance between (x1, y1) and (x2, y2) is the square root of [(x2 - x1)^2 + (y2 - y1)^2].\nIt is Pythagoras theorem on the horizontal and vertical differences.\nThe mid-point is ((x1 + x2)/2, (y1 + y2)/2).\nThe point that divides the segment internally in the ratio m : n is ((m x2 + n x1)/(m + n), (m y2 + n y1)/(m + n)).\nThe points of trisection divide the segment in the ratio 1 : 2 and 2 : 1.\nThe centroid of a triangle is the average of its three vertices."
        }
      },
